{"Unhandled async rejections: deleteScheduledEmailReminder and deleteScheduledSMSReminder are called inside .forEach() without await, meaning the wrapping try/catch never catches their rejections and they become unhandled promise rejections that can crash the Node.js process": 0.9014351963996887, "Single try/catch blocks wrapping multiple sequential async operations (external API call + database deletion) create failure cascades: when the first operation throws, subsequent critical operations like deleting the database record are skipped, leaving orphaned records that cron jobs re-process": 0.8741819262504578, "Inconsistent immediateDelete usage for email reminder cancellation between booking cancellation and rescheduling - handleCancelBooking.ts omits the flag while handleNewBooking.ts passes immediateDelete: true, meaning cancelled bookings may still receive email reminders if the cron hasn't processed the record before SendGrid fires it": 0.9249427318572998, "Missing method: WorkflowMethods.EMAIL filter in the remindersToCancel query causes cancelled SMS reminders to be picked up and their Twilio SID sent to SendGrid API as a batch_id, causing API failures. Since the entire cancellation loop is in a single try-catch, one failure aborts processing of all subsequent reminders": 0.9667508006095886}